# Jaguar XJS coupe, 1975-1996.
#
# The XJS: the long-lived V12 grand tourer with the low roofline, the
# buttressed rear quarter and the broad, flat tail. The pre-facelift
# 1975-1991 body is modelled; the 1991 facelift with the larger rear lamps and
# body-colour rear bumper is not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XJS
#
# Dimensions 4.870 x 1.793 x 1.270 m, wheelbase 2.591 m (pre-HE car).
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of a 1975 car built on
# 18 June 1975, plus front and rear three-quarters and a four-lamp headlamp
# detail. All four images are pre-facelift; the US four-lamp detail is of
# unstated year and is used only for the lamp arrangement.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period UK document was sighted. Black, Signal Red,
# British Racing Green and Silver are period Jaguar names recorded as context.
# Weights 10, 8, 6, 6, total 30, reflecting the model's long UK life,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 240 km/h. Comfort 90/465, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 90. Classes 3,4.
# Dates September 1975 to April 1996 production, road tail staggered
# 2010-2013.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-xjs.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-xjs.dae. References: citycars/references/jaguar-xjs/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pre-facelift 1975-1991 body is modelled. The side
# photograph is oblique, so the comparison camera was matched to it. Buttress,
# lamp and bumper detail is simplified at sprite scale. The four-lamp headlamp
# arrangement follows the detail photograph.


obj=citycar
name=JaguarXJS(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

